        "notes": "Choosing a branch defaults the base to main/master, so the list is the branch's own commits plus a 'Whole branch' row (hidden when there are none, or while searching). The list gives each subject two lines and moves the gloss/review marks to the detail line as small text, because pills left the subject too little room to tell commits apart. The selection lives in the URL hash. The frame is not sandboxed: sandbox=allow-scripts rendered a blank frame, and the view page has its own nonce CSP. Starts on wip when a snapshot exists. Commit search needs a few lines outside the search group (the q parameter in loadLog, the empty-result message), which are counted here. Load more is here because without it a branch with no base (such as main) can't be browsed past its newest 100 commits; Refresh and the deleted-branch fallback are in ary-conveniences, and the 'none' base option is in the picker (ary-search)."
